## Context Management
- Only read files explicitly mentioned or directly relevant to the task
- Never read the entire codebase unless asked
- Focus on one file at a time when possible
- Stop and ask before exploring more than 3 files

## Response Style
- Be concise, no explanations unless asked
- No summaries at the end of tasks
- Skip "I will now..." preambles, just do the task
- No suggestions for future improvements unless asked

## Code Changes
- Show only the changed code, not the entire file
- Make targeted edits, not full rewrites
- Ask for clarification before large refactors

## Task Execution
- Break large tasks into steps and confirm before proceeding
- If unsure about scope, ask one focused question first
